00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:35.050
They're old school in their thinking.

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.750
They haven't calibrated the
extreme nature of the internet.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:38.583
Too many people are trying

00:11:38.583 --> 00:11:40.603
to hold onto a secret that doesn't exist.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.210
And so what that does is
it makes them religious

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:46.510
about defense when it's
never been more important

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:47.623
to go on the offense.

00:11:48.835 --> 00:11:49.930
- [Crystal] Okay.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.443
- But that's a tough play because,

00:11:52.443 --> 00:11:54.560
I don't think you walking in to the room

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:55.760
is gonna convince them.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:57.200
Do you know what I mean?

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.240
- [Crystal] Right, and
I don't think so either.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.140
- But maybe they'll watch this full clip

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:03.270
whenever I put it up in full in a month,

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:04.710
and maybe that will get them going.

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:05.956
Because they're not sitting on anything.

00:12:05.956 --> 00:12:07.690
- [Crystal] I'm famous now?

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:10.010
- Yes, this whole video's going out.

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:10.980
You're famous now.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.033
- [Crystal] Yes!
(laughs)

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.300
- So, listen, that's just the way it is.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:19.750
Most companies, when they hit
a level where they're happy

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:21.380
they try to go on defense when they think

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.810
they're sitting on a secret.

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:24.310
But they're not sitting
on as big of a secret

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:25.143
as they think.

00:12:26.676 --> 00:12:28.171
- [Crystal] Okay, alright.

00:12:28.171 --> 00:12:29.640
- The inter-media would
be smaller not bigger

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:31.640
if I held on to all of these good ideas.

00:12:33.884 --> 00:12:35.550
- [Crystal] True, very true.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:36.383
Very, very true.

00:12:36.383 --> 00:12:37.760
- Alright, this was a lot of fun.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.660
See what happens when
you ask on the internet?

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.493
Shit happens.

00:12:40.493 --> 00:12:43.140
- [Crystal] Yes, oh my
god, I love you, Gary!

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.780
Thank you so much for taking the time.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:47.890
I'm so, so grateful that you
took the time out of your day.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:49.860
- No worries, take care, goodbye.

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.093
- [Crystal] Alright, bye.

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.256
- Keep on tweeting.

00:12:53.256 --> 00:12:56.589
(heartfelt piano plays)

